//! to surfaces. Floaters are a common artifact in 3D Gaussian splatting that appear as floating
//! blobs or structures disconnected from the actual scene geometry.
//!
//! Method:
//! - Render 360° orbit video around reconstruction
//! - Manual inspection for floating blobs and artifacts
//! - Render depth maps to check for isolated depth discontinuities
//!
//! Pass Criteria:
//! - No significant floaters visible in standard views
//! - Floaters documented if present with severity rating
//!
//! Severity if Found: Medium to High depending on severity
//!
//! ## How to Run This Test
//!
//! This is a MANUAL verification test that requires visual inspection of orbit renderings
//! and depth maps to identify floating artifacts.
//!
//! ### Quick Verification (Single Scene)
//!
//! For development/testing, use a scene from Mip-NeRF 360:
//!
//! ```bash
//! # Step 1: Train a model (or use existing trained model)
//! cargo build --release
//! ./target/release/sugar-train \
//!   --preset full \
//!   --dataset-root datasets/bicycle \
//!   --out-dir runs/floater_test_bicycle
//!
//! # Step 2: Run floater detection script generation test
//! cargo test --release tc_e2e_010_floater_generate_orbit_script -- --nocapture --ignored
//!
//! # Step 3: Render 360° orbit around reconstruction
//! python scripts/render_orbit_floater_detection.py \
//!   --model runs/floater_test_bicycle/model_final.gs \
//!   --dataset-root datasets/bicycle \
//!   --output runs/floater_test_bicycle/floater_detection \
//!   --frames 360 \
//!   --elevation 0
//!
//! # Step 4: Create video from rendered frames
//! ffmpeg -framerate 30 -i runs/floater_test_bicycle/floater_detection/frame_%04d.png \
//!   -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -crf 18 \
//!   runs/floater_test_bicycle/floater_orbit.mp4
//!
//! # Step 5: Manual inspection
//! # Watch the video and check:
//! # - No floating blobs visible in orbit video
//! # - No disconnected structures away from surfaces
//! # - Check depth maps for isolated depth discontinuities
//! # - Document any floaters with severity rating
//! ```
//!
//! ### Full Verification (All Scenes)
//!
//! For comprehensive testing, evaluate floater detection across all Mip-NeRF 360 scenes:
//!
//! ```bash
//! # Generate floater detection reports for all scenes
//! for scene in bicycle garden stump room counter kitchen bonsai; do
//!   echo "Evaluating floaters for $scene..."
//!   python scripts/render_orbit_floater_detection.py \
//!     --model runs/e2e_001_${scene}/model_final.gs \
//!     --dataset-root datasets/$scene \
//!     --output runs/e2e_001_${scene}/floater_detection \
//!     --frames 360 \
//!     --elevation 0
//!
//!   ffmpeg -framerate 30 -i runs/e2e_001_${scene}/floater_detection/frame_%04d.png \
//!     -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -crf 18 \
//!     runs/e2e_001_${scene}/floater_orbit.mp4
//! done
//! ```
//!
//! ### Alternative Camera Elevations
//!
//! Test floater detection from different viewing angles:
//!
//! ```bash
//! # Ground level orbit (elevation = 0)
//! python scripts/render_orbit_floater_detection.py \
//!   --model <model.gs> \
//!   --dataset-root <dataset> \
//!   --output <output_dir> \
//!   --elevation 0 \
//!   --frames 360
//!
//! # Elevated view (elevation = 30 degrees above)
//! python scripts/render_orbit_floater_detection.py \
//!   --model <model.gs> \
//!   --dataset-root <dataset> \
//!   --output <output_dir> \
//!   --elevation 30 \
//!   --frames 360
//!
//! # Top-down view (elevation = 90 degrees)
//! python scripts/render_orbit_floater_detection.py \
//!   --model <model.gs> \
//!   --dataset-root <dataset> \
//!   --output <output_dir> \
//!   --elevation 90 \
//!   --frames 180
//! ```
//!
//! ### Floater Types to Check
//!
//! The orbit rendering script helps identify several types of floating artifacts:
//!
//! 1. **Disconnected Blobs**
//!    - Gaussian clusters floating in empty space
//!    - Not attached to any surface
//!    - Often semi-transparent or low-opacity
//!
//! 2. **Stretched Gaussians**
//!    - Long, thin Gaussians bridging gaps between surfaces
//!    - "String-like" artifacts connecting unrelated geometry
//!    - May appear as visual artifacts during orbit
//!
//! 3. **Sky/Background Floaters**
//!    - Gaussians floating in background regions
//!    - Often appear as "clouds" or "fog" in empty space
//!    - Visible against uniform sky backgrounds
//!
//! 4. **Depth Discontinuity Floaters**
//!    - Visible in depth maps as isolated patches
//!    - Depth values inconsistent with surrounding geometry
//!    - Appear as disconnected regions in depth visualization
//!
//! ### Manual Inspection Checklist
//!
//! When reviewing orbit videos and depth maps for floaters, check for:
//!
//! 1. **Visual Inspection - RGB Renders**
//!    - Watch full orbit video for floating blobs
//!    - Check for semi-transparent artifacts in empty space
//!    - Look for "string-like" connections between surfaces
//!    - Verify background regions are clean (no fog/clouds)
//!
//! 2. **Depth Map Inspection**
//!    - Check for isolated depth patches (disconnected from surfaces)
//!    - Verify depth continuity on surfaces
//!    - Look for sudden depth discontinuities in empty space
//!    - Depth floaters appear as disconnected regions
//!
//! 3. **Severity Assessment**
//!    - **Low**: Minor floaters, barely visible, small count
//!    - **Medium**: Noticeable floaters, visible in some views, affects quality
//!    - **High**: Significant floaters, highly visible, severely impacts quality
//!
//! 4. **Documentation**
//!    - Count approximate number of floaters
//!    - Note which views show floaters most clearly
//!    - Describe floater characteristics (size, opacity, location)
//!    - Assign severity rating based on visual impact
//!
//! 5. **Pass/Fail Criteria**
//!    - **Pass**: No significant floaters, or only minor low-severity artifacts
//!    - **Marginal**: Some medium-severity floaters, but quality still acceptable
//!    - **Fail**: High-severity floaters that significantly degrade visual quality
//!
//! ## Implementation Notes
//!
//! This test provides infrastructure for floater detection but requires manual visual
//! inspection because:
//! - Floaters are subjective and context-dependent
//! - Visual impact varies by scene complexity and viewing angle
//! - Depth discontinuities may be legitimate scene features
//! - Human inspection is best judge of "significant" floaters
//!
//! The test generates helper scripts for:
//! - Rendering full 360° orbit at multiple elevations
//! - Creating video sequences for easy visual inspection
//! - (Future) Rendering depth maps for discontinuity detection
//! - Documenting floater locations and severity
//!
//! ## Current Status
//!
//! This test provides:
//! 1. Dataset verification (checks that test datasets exist)
//! 2. Script generation for orbit rendering
//! 3. Documentation for manual inspection workflow
//! 4. (Future) Depth map rendering for automated floater hints

